/-!
# Sylow and transfer-kernel certificates for the second Held candidate

Positive words and generator transitions enumerate the two previously specified
generated subgroups inside the actual permutation carrier. Every transition and
word equation is checked by kernel reduction. Distinctness comes from the shared
384-element enumeration. This proves their orders, the Sylow property, and the
normality and relative index of the transfer kernel.

The tables are generated by `source/generate_structure.py`, using composition
`(a * b)(i) = a(b(i))`. They are certificates for the proposed transfer argument
in Huppert--Blackburn III, XII.1.18(b), p.314, citing Held (1968), pp.436--449.
They do not assert the remaining intrinsic-radical subgroup classification.
-/

